cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use kicad-splitplane in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "kicad-splitplane: one continuous copper zone per supply net for KiCad power layers"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tuzlak
    given-names: Aleksandar
    affiliation: ETH Zurich
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/atuzlak/kicad-splitplane"
url: "https://people.ee.ethz.ch/~atuzlak/kicad-splitplane.html"
abstract: >-
  Splits a KiCad power layer into exactly one continuous copper zone per
  supply net, computed from the nets' vias and through-hole pads, and writes
  the zones into the board. KiCad 9/10 plugin, command-line tool, Python
  library and MCP server.
keywords:
  - KiCad
  - PCB design
  - power plane
  - split plane
  - EDA
